  "|Based on Abubakar Gimba's Witnesses to Tears: \nThe stealing of three thousand naira by the messenger and the manner of its presentation can be interpreted as Gimba's|sentimental attachment to money|approbation of stealing|condemnation of social injustice|justification of social vices": "set-african-prose",
  "|Based on George Orwell's Animal Farm: \nIn the novel, 'animalism' is a system of thought that emphasizes|conformity|equality|animality|disparity": "set-non-african-prose",
  "|Based on George Orwell's Animal Farm: \nThe dominant technique in the book is|irony|foreshadowing|symbolism|reminiscence": "set-non-african-prose",
