  "|Based on Oliver Goldsmith's She Stoops to Conquer: \nThe major thematic preoccupation of the play is|the constraints on parental obligations|the problems of class and English mannerisms|the presentation of a mannerless society|changing the traditional view about English comedy": "set-non-african-drama",
  "|Based on Oliver Goldsmith's She Stoops to Conquer: \nMiss Hardcastle is able to 'conquer' at the end of the play because of her|indiscretion|beauty|wit|brawn": "set-non-african-drama",
  "|Based on Oliver Goldsmith's She Stoops to Conquer: \nOne of the enriching features of the play is the|matchmaking attempts by Mrs. Hardcastle|manipulation of appearance and reality|use of rural and urban settings|lopsided resolution of conflicts": "set-non-african-drama",
