  "|Based on J.C. de Graft's Sons and Daughters: \n'Everything in this room outrages my sense of beauty, undermines my will to create pictures of lasting appeal...' The speaker in the quotation above is|happy|frustrated|excited|tired": "set-african-drama",
  "|Based on William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet: \n'Farewell! God knows when we shall meet again.\nI have a faint cold fear thrills through my veins,\nThat almost freezes up the heat of life:\nI'll call them back again to comfort me:\nNurse! What should she do here?\nMy dismal scene I needs must act alone.\nCome, vial.'\nThe intention of the speaker above is to|commit suicide|take a temporary harmful substance|commit murder|escape from harsh realities of life": "set-non-african-drama",
