  "|Based on the prescribed poems: \n'With a running stream and a water-mill beating the darkness,\nAnd three trees on the low sky.'\nIn the excerpt above from Eliot's Journey of the Magi, the dominant literary device is|oxymoron|personification|hyperbole|alliteration": "set-non-african-poetry",
